 - **two holes are closed**, each with its reproduction as the regression test: a command substitution inside double quotes no longer hides a command, and a quote closes as bash closes it (no escape inside single quotes; inside double quotes a quote is escaped only by an odd run of backslashes), so a quoted string ending in a backslash no longer hides what follows;
