+- **git's own words are read as git reads them** (BUG-045, docs/CHANGES.md, 2026-11-16; told to the owner as a material change after the gate, rule 58): a help word exempts a refusal only where git can do nothing but print help (exactly one help word after the subcommand, or `worktree remove` and one); the global options before the subcommand are read from a known list and any other one is refused as unreadable; every alias defined in the command (`-c alias.<x>=...`) is refused; a refused long option is read by any prefix git accepts (`--no-verify` from 6 characters, `--mirror` from 3, `--force` and its lease options from 4), and a short cluster holding `f` with `4` or `6` is a force push; `git config` naming `core.hooksPath` passes only in its read forms and in `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.
 What the guard defends is its threat-model row (docs/INVENTORY.md, Decisions, 2026-11-16): a command that names a refused action in its own words, under anything the guard reads, and the deadline; a deliberate reach that hides the action from the reading (an interpreter's code, a command a program takes from an option, its configuration or the environment, a child program's second parse under a crafted runtime or locale, a path written to reach an excluded launcher) is outside, recorded in docs/HARDENING.md, since `python -c` passes by design. Every wrapper, `eval`, here-document, alias, GraphQL-mutation and launcher-bypass refusal stays, as does a `gh api` read counting as a state change for rule 8's chain.
 
